%S A401306 4,32,36,108,216,256,392,400,432,500,900,968,1156,1296,1764,1800,1944,
%T A401306 2592,2700,2704,2916,3136,3200,3456,3600,4000,4356,4500,5184,5400,
%U A401306 6084,7056,8100,8464,8712,8788,9000,9216,10368,10584,10800,11236,12996,13068,13500
%N A401306 Powerful numbers preceded and followed by 3 consecutive squarefree numbers.
%C A401306 Powerful numbers k such that k-3, k-2, k-1, k+1, k+2, and k+3 are all squarefree numbers.
%C A401306 There are no four consecutive numbers that are all squarefree numbers since one of them must be divisible by 2^2 = 4. Therefore, all the terms in this sequence are multiples of 4, and thus even powerful numbers (A390010).
%C A401306 Subsequence of {4*A378172(n), n >= 1}.
%C A401306 The numbers of terms that do not exceed the (10^k)-th powerful number A376092(k), for k = 1, 2, ..., are 3, 22, 215, 2247, 22523, 225922, 2263994, 22663875, ... .
%C A401306 It appears that the relative asymptotic density of this sequence within the sequence of powerful numbers exists and equals 0.226... .
%H A401306 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401306/b401306.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401306 <a href="/index/Pow#powerful">Index entries for sequences related to powerful numbers</a>.
%t A401306 q[k_] := Divisible[k, 4] && AllTrue[FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]], # > 1 &] && AllTrue[k + {-3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3}, SquareFreeQ]; Select[Range[13500], q]
%o A401306 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k % 4 || !ispowerful(k), 0, my(v = [-3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3]); for(i = 1, 6, if(!issquarefree(k + v[i]), return(0))); 1);
%Y A401306 Intersection of A001694 (or A390010) and A068088.
%Y A401306 A373689 is a subsequence.
%Y A401306 Cf. A005117, A078325, A376092, A378172, A387532.
